; =====================================================================
; cddl-fragments.cddl
;
; VERBATIM -- these are RFC 8742's own bytes. Every region below is the
; cached source lifted by line range, with the RFC's THREE-SPACE LEFT
; MARGIN INTACT, so this file is NOT parseable as CDDL: the margin is
; part of what is being preserved. The tool-readable companion is
; cddl-fragments-dedented.derived.cddl, which is derived and says so.
;
; Only the "; ---" region banners and this header are ours. Remove every
; line beginning with ";" and what is left is byte-identical to the
; corresponding source lines.
;
; THREE fragments, and none of them is the format. RFC 8742 ships no
; grammar for a CBOR Sequence and says so: §4.1, "Currently, CDDL does
; not provide for unadorned CBOR Sequences as a top-level subject of a
; specification." F02 and F03 are therefore ARRAY rules that the
; document asks a reader to read as sequence rules, corrected by an
; English comment -- which the comment lines inside them say in the
; source's own words. The candidate containers a specification of ours
; would actually write are in cbor-seq-container.derived.cddl, which is
; derived and says so.
;
; DO NOT CONCATENATE THE REGIONS. F02 and F03 both define my-sequence,
; DIFFERENTLY (F02's element is a bare choice, F03's is a byte string
; wrapping one). A naive concatenation is a CDDL file with a conflicting
; duplicate rule name, which RFC 8610 Appendix C makes an error. Each
; region is its own file.
;
; Source: RFC 8742, cached source sha256
;   4462966836b60f42ebae9b5f1d2a479c328e16f0380a3434311a083bccbce30e
; =====================================================================

; --- F01  §4.1  a CBOR Sequence INSIDE a byte string, via .cborseq
;     source lines 195-197   region sha256 db6109d27e15f12e64458c319aef88f65b3e24f0d8fe56ef14c2cf56c324410b
   my-embedded-cbor-seq = bytes .cborseq my-array
   my-array = [* my-element]
   my-element = my-foo / my-bar

; --- F02  §4.1  the top-level workaround: an array rule plus English text
;     source lines 206-209   region sha256 34f33fbcc624b1ff1ab63c1bc53ff2d77d9bf904800c5ba1cb62c79dfb86ebbc
   ; This defines an array, the elements of which are to be used
   ; in a CBOR Sequence:
   my-sequence = [* my-element]
   my-element = my-foo / my-bar

; --- F03  §4.3  the skipping optimisation: each element wrapped in a byte string
;     source lines 245-249   region sha256 8c0a1bf5b3f27a17825f9ebb2de0f2658ef70e821db79a2c0d4ed515829fd6d1
   ; This defines an array of CBOR byte strings, the elements of which
   ; are to be used in a CBOR Sequence:
   my-sequence = [* my-element]
   my-element = bytes .cbor my-element-structure
   my-element-structure = my-foo / my-bar

